  "term": "female genitalia",
  "definition": "Female genitalia are the female copulatory or reproductive structures. In the cited Drosophila study, these structures included species-specific parts that contact male genital structures during mating and may coevolve with them, with some possibly serving as protective shields against harmful male features.",
